From 7bb9254523898142c911ce4c51d13d55c4ce78df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 19:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rpi: initialize buffer index before stream lookup

GCC 15 cannot infer from ASSERT(stream) that index was assigned by the
preceding loop and reports maybe-uninitialized errors. Initialize index to
the value getBufferId() uses for no matching buffer. The assertion continues
to catch a buffer that does not belong to any stream.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 src/libcamera/pipeline/rpi/pisp/pisp.cpp | 2 +-
 src/libcamera/pipeline/rpi/vc4/vc4.cpp   | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/rpi/pisp/pisp.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/rpi/pisp/pisp.cpp
index 53fa026a..a115579e 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/rpi/pisp/pisp.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/rpi/pisp/pisp.cpp
@@ -1797 +1797 @@ void PiSPCameraData::beOutputDequeue(FrameBuffer *buffer)
-	int index;
+	int index = 0;
diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/rpi/vc4/vc4.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/rpi/vc4/vc4.cpp
index 1d6a7f7c..b9d5d895 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/rpi/vc4/vc4.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/rpi/vc4/vc4.cpp
@@ -753 +753 @@ void Vc4CameraData::unicamBufferDequeue(FrameBuffer *buffer)
-	unsigned int index;
+	unsigned int index = 0;
